/**
 * BCS bytes written by Move itself: `sui::bcs::to_bytes` of real `ghosts::ghosts::Game`,
 * `ghosts::account::Account`, `Seat`, `State`, `Ending` and `history::Record` values, taken
 * from a throwaway `sui move test` on a scratch copy of the package at the working tree the
 * SDK was aligned with (never added to the repo; the printer is `fixtures-printer.move.txt`).
 * The `game*` ones but `gameScript*` are the contract's own test fixture: Alice (the player who waited, goes first) and Bob on `map::demo_1`, one armed
 * recruit a side (Plasma rifle, Medium armor, frag grenade), Alice's account `0x63d9...3975`,
 * Bob's `0xdba7...7a97`. These pin the SDK's layout to the contract's: a changed Move struct
 * fails here, where a round-trip through the SDK's own schema never would.
 *
 * `gameScript0` to `gameScript10` are a scripted match on an empty 8x8 map, four recruits a side,
 * with both grenades thrown, a refresh, expiries and a kill of a dazed recruit (see
 * `parity.test.ts`).
 */

